{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff from a second (epic-driver) session that was working this story in parallel and is now STANDING DOWN — this ticket is yours. Posting findings + a harvestable patch so none of it has to be rediscovered.\n\n## Three content-DESTROYING pandoc behaviours a real-prose corpus caught\nAll measured on pandoc 3.6.1 (the binary bundled in the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel), rendering `-f commonmark -t jira --wrap=none`. Each one silently corrupts content, and none is visible from hand-written examples:\n\n1. **pandoc escapes punctuation INSIDE code spans.** `` `-> <- <-> =>` `` renders as `{{\\-> <\\- <-> =>}}`. Pre-substituting arrows correctly spares code, and pandoc corrupts it anyway on the way out. A \"skip code when substituting\" rule alone is NOT sufficient.\n2. **pandoc DELETES HTML comments.** A lone `<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->` renders to the EMPTY STRING. That is rebar's own reconciler echo marker, so this is a correctness bug, not a cosmetic one — a dropped marker breaks loop-breaking.\n3. **A naive arrow rule corrupts the HTML-comment terminator.** `-->` contains `->`, so substitution rewrites it to `-→`. Fix: match `<!--` and `-->` FIRST and map them to themselves so the inner arrow is consumed by the delimiter.\n\nMitigation that covers all three without enumerating pandoc's quirks: a **post-render code-preservation check** — after converting a unit, require every code fragment of the source to appear verbatim in the output, else fall back to that unit's original Markdown. This converts unpredictable escaping into a safe fallback. Recommend adding it whatever the implementation shape.\n\nAlso worth keeping: pandoc's jira writer emits a stray `{anchor:}` after EVERY heading (`h1. {anchor:}Title`) — it is not content and needs stripping; and re-rendering already-wiki text as Markdown is destructive (`{{x}}` → `\\{\\{x\\}\\}`, `{noformat}` dissolves), so a unit that already looks like wiki should pass through.\n\n## Harvestable implementation: /tmp/pony-swan-271c.patch\nComplete, gates-green, NOT pushed and NOT committed anywhere. 10 files / ~1,010 insertions:\n- `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` (318 LOC) — segmenting renderer: blank-line/fence-aware split, safe/table/verbatim classification, code-aware arrow substitution, `{noformat}` table wrap, `{anchor:}` strip, post-render code-preservation check, already-wiki passthrough, identity fallback when pandoc is absent.\n- `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py` + `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/` — deterministic generator and a scrubbed 178-body fixture (29 code-arrow / 29 table / 120 prose), every shard <=127 KB.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py` + `test_wiki_render_corpus.py` — 57 tests passing.\n- `pyproject.toml` `wiki` extra (`pypandoc-binary==1.15`, pinned exactly) + dev pin so CI actually exercises the path; registered in `src/rebar/_optional.py`.\n- `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` — the vocabulary gate scans fixture CONTENT and fails on historical ticket prose, so the fixture directory needs excluding (it is captured data, not authored text). Expect this failure otherwise.\n\nMeasured over that fixture: 92.7% of bodies and 98.4% of characters render rich; 0 code-arrow fragments lost; 31/31 table bodies still tables; all HTML comments survive. `make lint` and `make typecheck` both green; `wiki_render.py` is 318 LOC (inside the 200-500 target, under the 800 cap).\n\nApologies for the earlier plan-material churn — a description edit of mine landed and was superseded by yours; that session is now stood down and will make no further edits here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786570441572791001,"uuid":"e1143a3f-d54a-4f33-b6e2-d08ad7c00039"}